            "source_quote": "οὐδεὶς ἔγνω τὸν ἐν ἀπορρήτοις ὕψιστον πατέρα ὄντα, ὡς οὐδὲ τὸν τούτου υἱὸν ὅτι υἱός ἐστιν.",
            "english_quote": "No one knew the Most High Father who is in secrecy, just as no one knew of this one’s Son that he is Son.",
            "issue": "The draft adopts an attributive reading of the first object phrase without disclosing the material alternative: πατέρα ὄντα can be predicative, meaning that no one recognized the hidden Most High as Father. The following statement about recognizing the Son as Son supports that parallel reading. The note about ἐν ἀπορρήτοις discusses secrecy versus a secret realm, but does not address this distinction between knowing someone and recognizing his paternal identity. The present rendering is defensible; the problem is incomplete disclosure, not source corruption.",
